{#-
  Everything is open to crawlers. What a reader can reach, a search engine can
  index — the pages are the point of the site, and there is nothing here behind
  a door.

  The pages that should not turn up in results say so on their own, with a
  `noindex` tag written from the same `noIndex` flag that keeps them out of the
  sitemap. That is the mechanism that actually works: a `Disallow` here asks a
  crawler not to *fetch* a page, which leaves it free to list the URL anyway
  from a link somewhere else, and forbidding the fetch is what stops it ever
  reading the `noindex` that would have kept it out.

  The sitemap is named absolutely, which the spec asks for and several crawlers
  require.
-#}
